<title>UK: ICO coffee exports top 80 mln in 12 mths to April.</title>
<headline>ICO coffee exports top 80 mln in 12 mths to April.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Coffee Organization (ICO) said on Thursday exporting members' exports topped 80.74 million 60-kg bags in the 12 months to April 1997, up sharply from 71.36 million in the same 1996 period,</p>
<p>In April, exports fell to 7.01 million bags from 7.40 million in March but up from 6.67 million in April 1996.</p>
<p>In the first seven months of the current 1996/97 coffee year to April, total exports were up at 50.07 million from 43.49 million in the same 1995/96 period.</p>
<p>Latest ICO export data, in thousand bags, included --</p>
<p>		   April 97   April 96  Oct/April 96/97 Oct/April</p>
<p>95/96</p>
<p>    Brazil	 1,405	 732	11,606	    6,345</p>
<p>    Colombia	 822	 855	 6,777	    6,709</p>
<p>    Guatemala	575	 438	 3,261	    2,479</p>
<p>    El Salvador    452	 399	 2,073	    1,480</p>
<p>    Mexico	   447	 527	 3,708	    3,471</p>
<p>    Indonesia	246	 347	 2,708	    2,484</p>
<p>    Uganda	   268	 394	 2,944	    2,758</p>
<p>    Vietnam	  307	 399	 4,155	    2,971</p>
<p>    Ethiopia	 310	 202	 1,096		808</p>
<p>    Ivory Coast    389	 463	 1,367	    1,551</p>
<p>-- Jalil Hamid, London newsroom +44 171 542 4985</p>
</text>
